WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.950
On Sweden's High Coast and
Finland's Kvarken Archipelago,

2
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.110
the land is still rising, by
around 0.9 metres a century.

3
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:14.290
New islands keep emerging, and
old shorelines now sit far inland.

4
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:21.470
Yet worldwide, sea level rose 3.7
millimetres a year between 2006 and 2018.

5
00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.670
So how can one coast climb out
of the sea while others drown?

6
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.110
Is the Baltic draining away?

7
00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.170
In this mission, you'll find out what
has been driving global sea-level rise.

8
00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:36.710
Then you'll read the coast
itself: raised beaches,

9
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.210
relict cliffs and the
fjords of western Norway.

10
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.370
Your mission: explain how the Gulf of
Bothnia coast can rise out of the sea while

11
00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.990
other coasts drown.
